				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fleetingrain" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5522240); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5522240&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606380111" alt="FleetingRain" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5522240)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fleetingrain" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5522240); return false;" >FleetingRain</a></span> <span class="odate time_1563974235 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">24 Jul 2019 13:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4313757">
									

<p>As others have said, this feels like two SCPs woven into one. I think you should either split them (the octopus+submarine already work together greatly) or cut some of the fat here.</p>
<p>SCP-1485 is really unnecessary, and even detrimental to this story I believe. We have a bajillion parallel universes in the canon, why do we need to check on the normie one to realize the Beatles have gone missing? Does it mean literally every other universe we know of also doesn't have them (so is 1485 really the &quot;correct&quot; one in having them)? No, nevermind that, why does the Foundation still have people in SCP-1485 if agents used to desert all the time?</p>
<p>I also don't really like how the Keter reveal was more &quot;told&quot; than &quot;shown&quot;. I'd like to see the Hindi woman in the interview throw more references to Beatles's lyrics so the reader would go &quot;hold up&quot; and realize something was going on; bonus points if Agent Nandasiri didn't catch the references, so we'd know something (like a whole band lmao) was amiss.</p>
<p>If your intent with this article was to surprise the reader with the realization that the Beatles don't exist <em>anymore</em> (this is important because they <em>did</em> exist), I think you should try another approach. For example, maybe the inhabitants of the kelp garden/submarine still know about the Beatles (this one would let the Keter version be kept). Maybe the Foundation never really cracks open the mystery of this one SCP, but the readers realize what's going on. Or maybe the octopus is Ringo. Anything but the heavy crossover exposition you went with here.</p>

							</div>

								
